; exclude_integer_model: EXCLUDE on an integer {0, 1, 2} model raises NonBinaryModel.
;
; EXCLUDE writes a mutual-exclusion penalty on variables 0 and 1, and spec/xqvm/HLF.md derives
; every constraint expansion under x^2 = x, which fails for spin variables
; and for integer variables with k > 2. The check follows the declared domain
; (only a model allocated by BQMX passes), so spec/xqvm/ISA.md has EXCLUDE raise NonBinaryModel instead. Every other
; operand is valid, so the domain check alone decides.

PUSH 4
PUSH 3
XQMX r0          ; integer model, k = 3, 4 variables
PUSH 0           ; i
PUSH 1           ; j
PUSH 5           ; penalty
EXCLUDE r0
HALT
